  "id": "cerebellar-gait",
  "term": "cerebellar gait",
  "definition": "Cerebellar gait is an abnormal pattern of walking caused by cerebellar ataxia. In this packet, it is linked to problems in cerebellar pathways involved in body-position sensing and balance-related vestibular function, and is described as a major clinical sign of FXTAS.",
